    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d211-a1">

                <pb facs="0362" n="266" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg266"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure A in No. 119.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Etheart to Mr. Bassett.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State for Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1872-03-22"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 22, 1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: It has come to my knowledge that a
                    protest, drawn up by Mr. Jastram, residing at Saint Marc, has been addressed to
                    you.</p>
                <p>In the name of my government, which I represent at the capital, I am ready to
                    give you all desirable information on the subject of this protest.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, I pray you, Mr. Minister, to accept the renewed assurance of my very
                    high consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>L. ETHÉART.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
